    rdf:value """against the gloom of the cupola. We discussed “ Manon Lescaut ” a good deal, and found it peculiarly wonderful because it was the first psychological presentation of a woman who could love and yet be “unfaithful”, regarding her body as a thing apart. Fafnir has the faculty of drawing B.B. out in a delightful way. I am reading  D’Annunzio’ s  Trionfo della Morte , and B.B. “Nell Horn” .
[London. Thursday. August 23. 1894]"""^^xsd:string ;
